"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Does GPU parallelism change how many of the 671 CAMELS catchments can get full Bayesian calibration instead of point optimization?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Each catchment calibrates independently, so GPU batching turns full Bayesian treatment of all 671 into a cheap throughput problem, not a blocker.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:sequential_part\",\"text\":\"Each catchment's posterior waits on one chain's 100,000 serial proposal-accept steps; four chains per catchment.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:method\",\"text\":\"none - the 671 catchments' four chains each are independent, so all 2,684 chains run side by side in one batched pass.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"One GPU gives >=20x over CPU and finishes all 671 in under an hour, so compute is the lever here.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Vectorized CPU finishes all 671 in a couple of hours, so throughput does not decide which catchments get full Bayesian treatment.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Time full Bayesian MCMC (4 chains x 1e5 iterations, R-hat<1.2) for 671 CAMELS catchments on one GPU versus a vectorized CPU and versus point optimization; measure whether GPU throughput decides how many catchments get full Bayesian treatment.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"Freitas et al. 2022 GPU-optimized a hydrological model's calibration to 20x CPU speedup, on one distributed model, not batched MCMC across many GR4J catchments [s_mgb].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_mgb\",\"url\":\"https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/performance-optimization-of-the-mgb-hydrological-model-for-multi-/\",\"quote\":\"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"No published result times batched GPU MCMC giving all 671 CAMELS catchments full Bayesian GR4J treatment, so the crossover is unmeasured [s_mgb].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_mgb\",\"url\":\"https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/performance-optimization-of-the-mgb-hydrological-model-for-multi-/\",\"quote\":\"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Reproduce airGR's GR4J: parameter set X=(165.05, 6.46, 422.50, 2.45) gives calibration NSE 0.495 on its example basin [s_airgr_nse].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_airgr_nse\",\"url\":\"https://hydrogr.github.io/airGR/page_3_param_sets_GR4J.html\",\"quote\":\"The Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency criterion computed on the calibration period is better (0.495)\"}],\"value\":0.495}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Shows GR4J only, not expensive distributed or hierarchical models; US CAMELS unless the optional global stretch runs; nothing about single-chain mixing limits.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_airgr_nse\",\"url\":\"https://hydrogr.github.io/airGR/page_3_param_sets_GR4J.html\",\"quote\":\"The Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency criterion computed on the calibration period is better (0.495)\",\"supports\":\"anchor_nse = 0.495\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_mgb\",\"url\":\"https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/performance-optimization-of-the-mgb-hydrological-model-for-multi-/\",\"quote\":\"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\",\"supports\":\"speedup_threshold = 20 (PROXY)\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:camels_n\",\"name\":\"CAMELS US catchments\",\"value\":671,\"unit\":\"catchments\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"We present a new data set of attributes for 671 catchments in the contiguous United States (CONUS) minimally impacted by human activities.\",\"page_setting\":\"Addor et al. 2017, HESS (CAMELS dataset)\",\"url\":\"https://hess.copernicus.org/articles/21/5293/2017/hess-21-5293-2017.html\"}
{\"ref\":\"num:dist_evals_per_catchment\",\"name\":\"evaluations to converge one 241-parameter distributed model\",\"value\":50000000,\"unit\":\"evaluations\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"quote\":\"Previous results presented by Keating et al. [2010] have shown that DREAM required about 50 million surrogate model evaluations to converge to a limiting parameter distribution\",\"page_setting\":\"Nevada Test Site 241-parameter groundwater model (Laloy & Vrugt 2012)\",\"url\":\"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011WR010608\"}

